IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1, PART 2 (PROVISIONS RELATING TO AUTHORITY, ss 3 and 4).
-- These rules state the 2024 consolidation. The Minister's directions and the Authority's non-liability are encoded for what they mean to a licensee and to a person who suffers loss.

§ `3. Directions by Minister`

-- src:885 | 3.—(1) The Minister may, after consultation with a person to whom
-- src:886 | this section applies, give to that person such directions as the Minister
-- src:887 | thinks fit as to the exercise by that person of that person’s functions
-- src:888 | under this Act.
@ref s 3(1) (src:885-888)
GIVEN `the Minister has consulted the person to whom the section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the Minister may give the person the directions the Minister thinks fit as to the exercise of its functions under this Act` MEANS
    `the Minister has consulted the person to whom the section applies`

-- src:890 | (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if it appears to the Minister to
-- src:891 | be requisite or expedient to do so —
-- src:893 | (a) when any public emergency occurs, in the public interest
-- src:894 | or in the interests of public security, national defence or
-- src:895 | relations with the government of another country; or
-- src:897 | (b) in order —
-- src:899 | (i) to discharge or facilitate the discharge of an
-- src:900 | obligation binding on the Government by virtue of
-- src:901 | its being a member of an international organisation
-- src:902 | or a party to an international agreement;
-- src:904 | (ii) to attain or facilitate the attainment of any other
-- src:905 | object the attainment of which is in the opinion of the
-- src:906 | Minister requisite or expedient in view of the
-- src:911 | Government being a member of such an organisation
-- src:912 | or a party to such an agreement; or
-- src:914 | (iii) to enable the Government to become a member of
-- src:915 | such an organisation or a party to such an agreement,
-- src:917 | the Minister may, after consultation with a person to whom this
-- src:918 | section applies, give such directions to that person as are necessary in
-- src:919 | the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 3(2) (src:890-919)
GIVEN `it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient to do so on a public emergency, in the public interest or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with another government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient to do so to discharge an obligation of the Government as a member of an international organisation or party to an international agreement, to attain an object so requisite, or to enable the Government to become a member or party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has consulted the person to whom the section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(2) the Minister may, after consultation, give the directions that are necessary in the circumstances` MEANS
    `the Minister has consulted the person to whom the section applies`
    AND (`it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient to do so on a public emergency, in the public interest or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with another government` OR `it appears to the Minister requisite or expedient to do so to discharge an obligation of the Government as a member of an international organisation or party to an international agreement, to attain an object so requisite, or to enable the Government to become a member or party`)

-- src:921 | (3) Any directions given under subsection (1) or (2) may include
-- src:922 | provisions for —
-- src:924 | (a) the prohibition or regulation of any broadcasting service;
-- src:926 | (b) the taking of, the control of or the use for official purposes
-- src:927 | of, all or any system and equipment used in the provision
-- src:928 | of any broadcasting service; and
-- src:930 | (c) the stopping, delaying and censoring of messages and the
-- src:931 | carrying out of any other purposes which the Minister
-- src:932 | thinks necessary.
@ref s 3(3) (src:921-932)
GIVEN `it is a provision for the prohibition or regulation of any broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a provision for the taking, control or use for official purposes of all or any system and equipment used in providing a broadcasting service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a provision for the stopping, delaying and censoring of messages, or any other purpose the Minister thinks necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(3) directions under subsection (1) or (2) may include this provision` MEANS
    IF `it is a provision for the prohibition or regulation of any broadcasting service` OR `it is a provision for the taking, control or use for official purposes of all or any system and equipment used in providing a broadcasting service` OR `it is a provision for the stopping, delaying and censoring of messages, or any other purpose the Minister thinks necessary`
    THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:934 | (4) A person to whom this section applies must give immediate
-- src:935 | effect to any directions given to the person under subsection (1) or (2)
-- src:936 | despite any other duty imposed on the person by or under this Act.
@ref s 3(4) (src:934-936)
GIVEN `directions have been given to the person under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(4) the person must give immediate effect to the directions despite any other duty under this Act` MEANS
    `directions have been given to the person under subsection (1) or (2)`

-- src:938 | (5) A person to whom this section applies must not disclose any
-- src:939 | directions given to the person under subsection (1) or (2) if the
-- src:940 | Minister notifies the person that the Minister is of the opinion that the
-- src:941 | disclosure of the directions is against the public interest.
@ref s 3(5) (src:938-941)
GIVEN `the Minister has notified the person that the Minister is of the opinion that disclosure of the directions is against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(5) the person must not disclose the directions` MEANS
    `the Minister has notified the person that the Minister is of the opinion that disclosure of the directions is against the public interest`

-- src:943 | (6) The Minister may —
-- src:945 | (a) pay compensation for any damage caused to a licensee by
-- src:946 | reason of its compliance with the Minister’s directions
-- src:947 | under subsection (3)(b); or
-- src:949 | (b) make grants to licensees for defraying or contributing
-- src:950 | towards any losses which they may sustain by reason of
-- src:951 | their compliance with the Minister’s directions under any
-- src:952 | other provisions of this section.
@ref s 3(6) (src:943-952)
GIVEN `it is compensation for damage caused to a licensee by reason of its compliance with directions under subsection (3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a grant to licensees to defray or contribute towards losses sustained by compliance with directions under other provisions of the section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(6) the Minister may pay this compensation or make this grant` MEANS
    IF `it is compensation for damage caused to a licensee by reason of its compliance with directions under subsection (3)(b)` OR `it is a grant to licensees to defray or contribute towards losses sustained by compliance with directions under other provisions of the section` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:957 | (7) Any sums required by the Minister for paying compensation or
-- src:958 | making grants under subsection (6) are to be paid out of the
-- src:959 | Consolidated Fund.
@ref s 3(7) (src:957-959)
GIVEN `it is a sum the Minister requires for paying compensation or making grants under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(7) the sum is paid out of the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `it is a sum the Minister requires for paying compensation or making grants under subsection (6)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:961 | (8) This section applies to the Authority and to any person who is a
-- src:962 | licensee.
@ref s 3(8) (src:961-962)
GIVEN `it is the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a person who is a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(8) the section applies to it` MEANS
    `it is the Authority` OR `it is a person who is a licensee`

-- src:964 | (9) If any doubt arises as to —
-- src:966 | (a) the existence of a public emergency; or
-- src:968 | (b) whether any act done under this section was in the public
-- src:969 | interest or in the interests of public security, national
-- src:970 | defence or relations with the government of another
-- src:971 | country,
-- src:973 | a certificate signed by the Minister is conclusive evidence of the
-- src:974 | matters stated in the certificate.
@ref s 3(9) (src:964-974)
GIVEN `a doubt arises as to the existence of a public emergency, or whether an act done under the section was in the public interest or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with another government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has signed a certificate stating the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(9) the Minister's certificate is conclusive evidence of the matters stated` MEANS
    IF `a doubt arises as to the existence of a public emergency, or whether an act done under the section was in the public interest or in the interests of public security, national defence or relations with another government` THEN JUST `the Minister has signed a certificate stating the matter` ELSE NOTHING

§ `4. Exclusion of liability of Authority for act or default of licensees`

-- src:978 | 4. The Authority shall not be liable in respect of any injury, loss or
-- src:979 | damage suffered by any person by reason of any act, default, neglect
-- src:980 | or otherwise of any licensee or of any agent or employee of the
-- src:981 | licensee.
@ref s 4 (src:978-981)
GIVEN `the person suffered injury, loss or damage by reason of an act, default, neglect or otherwise of a licensee or of its agent or employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4 the Authority is liable to the person for that injury, loss or damage` MEANS
    IF `the person suffered injury, loss or damage by reason of an act, default, neglect or otherwise of a licensee or of its agent or employee` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING
